 ],
 "literal": "Those who destroy what they have are not considered as living / The life of those who have nothing is more disgraceful than begging, thus / showing clearly his strength of resolve / he went, may you live, my friend, always / through the path of the spear-bearing bandits like the God of Death / who stay and linger on the path and kill those who pass by / where vultures watch for the stench of corpses / in the vast ancient wasteland, the path indeed without water.",
 "translation": "My friend, may you live long! He has departed, demonstrating clearly his firm resolve: 'Those who waste their existing wealth are not counted among the living, and the life of those who have nothing is more disgraceful than begging.' He has gone through the waterless path in the vast, ancient wasteland, where vultures watch for the stench of corpses of travelers killed by fierce bandits with murderous spears like Death itself, who lie in wait along the way.",
 "modern": "தோழியே! நீ வாழ்க! 'தம்மிடம் உள்ள பொருளை அழித்து வாழ்பவர்கள் உயிருடன் வாழ்பவர்களாகக் கருதப்பட மாட்டார்கள்; வறுமையில் வாடுபவர்களின் வாழ்க்கை இரந்து கேட்பதை விடவும் இழிவானது' என்று தான் கூறிய உறுதியைத் தெளிவாகக் காட்டிவிட்டு அவர் சென்றுவிட்டார். எமனைப் போன்ற கொலை செய்யும் வேலினை ஏந்திய மறவர்கள், வழியில் தங்கிச் செல்வோரைக் கொன்று குவித்ததால் உண்டான பிண நாற்றத்தை எதிர்நோக்கிப் பருந்துகள் காத்திருக்கும், நீர் இல்லாத, நீண்ட பழமையான பாலைநில வழியில்தான் அவர் சென்றுள்ளார்.",
 "explanation": "The heroine is speaking to her confidante (tōḻi) after her lover has departed to earn wealth. She recalls his words about the importance of earning wealth: that wasting existing resources is not true living, and living in poverty is worse than begging. To prove his resolve, he has journeyed through a perilous desert path (pālai tiṇai). This path is described as waterless and ancient, infested with ruthless bandits who, like the God of Death, lie in wait to kill travelers, leaving corpses that attract vultures. The harshness of the landscape reflects the immense difficulty of his quest and the strength of his determination, while highlighting the heroine's deep anxiety for his safety.",
